    "created_at": "2016-09-13T20:17:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-13T20:17:58Z",
    "body": "Serialize does not make a copy of shared memory, neither for postMessage nor for IDB. It just serializes to the record of the form  { [[Type]]: \"SharedArrayBuffer\", [[BackingData]]: the [[ArrayBufferData]] of the source }. When this is Deserialized by postMessage, it just creates a new SAB with the pointer to [[BackingData]]. When IDB performs its implementation-specific records-to-bytes translation, it makes a copy of the data.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
