    "created_at": "2016-09-14T05:08:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-14T05:08:40Z",
    "body": "And IDB doesn't make a copy of the data necessarily. For `File` objects it just stores a pointer, as far as I know. If it made a copy of the data it would do more than structured cloning offers and I don't think it does that (which is the main reason why we don't want `SharedArrayBuffer` there I think, presumably this also applies to the Notifications API).\n",
